What: advance RAM KMS capture deadlines from their original phase with
sleep_until, instead of resetting the deadline after a slow frame. Late
frames still perform a real acquisition. No busy-wait or affinity change.
Status: upstreamable pacing fix, carried downstream pending wider testing.
Evidence: 6b81298/e1180ed; /tmp/h700-sun/convert.md (2026-10-22): combined
row-pair/pacing/FIFO experiment delivered 600 acquisitions in all 27 windows.
Removal: equivalent upstream pacing or evidence of unsafe catch-up load.
Cost: a long stall causes immediate real catch-up acquisitions.

